  "title": "Covid-19 Vaccines and Miscarriage: What the Evidence Really Shows",
  "summary": "False claims about Covid-19 vaccines and miscarriage are circulating online again, fueled by renewed debate over data collected during the early stages of the pandemic. One of the most widely repeated claims suggests that Covid-19 vaccination was associated with an 82% miscarriage rate. However, that figure comes from a flawed interpretation of an early vaccine safety study and does not represent the actual miscarriage risk among vaccinated pregnant women. The issue has resurfaced following the",
